:"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:43:32Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:43:32+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:43:32+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/output_0d77a839.md`\nTotal Lines: 32\nTotal Bytes: 2342\nShowing lines 1 to 32\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Worker Output: 0d77a839\n2: \n3: ## Task\n4: Settle an open graph-theory conjecture in Lean 4: `(nontrivial) ⇒ (radius + 1) ≤ roman_domination_number` by proving `prove_e20263a9` in `Challenge_e20263a9.lean`.\n5: \n6: ## Mathematical Analysis & Settlement\n7: 1. **Direction**: Universally **TRUE** (`prove_e20263a9`).\n8: 2. **Computational Evidence**:\n9:    - 0 counterexamples across 1,252 graphs up to $n=6$ (all connected graphs).\n10:    - 0 counterexamples across all non-isomorphic trees up to $n=16$.\n11:    - 0 counterexamples across hundreds of random graphs and trees tested with MILP.\n12: 3. **Analytical Proof**:\n13:    - For Roman dominating function $f$:\n14:      - If no vertex has label 2: $\\text{weight}(f) \\ge |V| \\ge \\text{radius}(G) + 1$.\n15:      - If unique vertex $c$ has label 2: ball of radius 1 around $c$ contains $c$ and all vertices labeled 0. The complement has size at most $|V_1| = \\text{weight}(f) - 2$. By strict ball expansion, $\\text{ballWithin}(G, \\text{weight}(f) - 1, c) = V$, so $\\text{eccentricity}(c) \\le \\text{weight}(f) - 1$, implying $\\text{radius}(G) + 1 \\le \\text{weight}(f)$.\n16:      - For $|V_2| \\ge 2$: centers in a spanning tree are at distance $\\le 3$, yielding $\\text{radius}(G) \\le \\lfloor \\frac{3|V_2|-1}{2} \\rfloor + |V_1| \\le 2|V_2| + |V_1| - 1 = \\text{weight}(f) - 1$.\n17: \n18: ## Formal Verification & Deliverables\n19: 1. **22 Kernel-Checked Lemmas**:\n20:    - Proved in `Challenge_e20263a9.lean` and `scratch.lean`.\n21:    - Includes key theorems:\n22:      - `radius_add_one_le_card`: $\\text{radius}(G) + 1 \\le |V|$.\n23:      - `mem_ballWithin_of_walk`: Endpoint of any walk is in $\\text{ballWithin}$ at walk length.\n24:      - `ballWithin_eq_univ_of_forall_walk`: Universal reachability from bounded walks.\n25:      - `card_ballWithin_add` and `ballWithin_eq_univ_of_card_add`: Multi-step ball growth and universal convergence.\n26:      - `card_le_romanWeight_of_no_two`: Weight bound $|V| \\le \\text{romanWeight}(f)$ when no 2 is present.\n27:      - `radius_add_one_le_romanWeight_of_card_le`: Transitive bound when $|V| \\le \\text{romanWeight}(f)$.\n28:      - `mem_ballWithin_one_of_adj` & `mem_ballWithin_one_self`: 1-step ball contains center and all neighbors.\n29: 2. **Verification**:\n30:    - `/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh Challenge_e20263a9.lean` exits with code 0.\n31:    - Standard axioms only: `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`.\n32: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":1250,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:43:32Z","thinking":"**Identifying Proof Case Structure**\n\nThe proof examines the case where the cardinality of V₂ is greater than or equal to 2, utilizing the spanning tree argument to bound the radius. A crucial step is to analyze when case distinction is needed in the Lean proof. The proof utilizes a function `f` mapping vertices to `Fin 3` and a hypothesis `hf`.\n\n\n**Examining Graph Properties Deduction**\n\nThe analysis proceeds by contradiction, considering cases based on the relationship between the graph's radius and the roman weight. The critical inequality focuses on establishing radius G + 1 ≤ romanWeight f when either `Fintype.card V ≤ romanWeight f`, `radius G ≤ 1`, or `romanWeight f ≤ 2`. The cases converge to where `romanWeight f < card V`, `radius G ≥ 2`, and `romanWeight f ≥ 3`.\n\nA vertex labeling function f is assumed; it then explores the existence of a vertex labeled with 2. The analysis identifies key implications depending on whether zero, one, or at least two vertices receive a label of 2. Focus shifts towards a potentially critical subcase when at least two vertices are labeled with 2.\n\nConsider the sub-case where at least two vertices have a label of 2. Deductions involve proving `romanWeight(f) ≥ 4` and potentially reducing the problem to establishing whether `radius(G) ≤ 3`. It is necessary to determine if such a high radius is possible when `romanWeight f` is small and two vertices are labeled 2.\n\n\n**Analyzing Radius Bound Contradiction**\n\nIf the graph's radius is at least 4, then the number of vertices is at least 5. It cannot have a roman weight of 4 if the radius is greater than or equal to 4. Assume the roman weight is 4; two vertices must have label 2, and all others have label 0. Thus, the vertex set becomes the union of closed neighborhoods of these two vertices.\n\nExamining the structure reveals that the distance between any two vertices in the set is at most 3. Therefore, if the radius is at least 4 and the roman weight equals 4, there's a contradiction, since the radius would be at most 3. If they are adjacent the radius is at most 2.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/scratch_rdn.lean","StartLine":1,"toolAction":"Viewing file","toolSummary":"View scratch_rdn.lean"}}]}
{"step_index":1251,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:43:38Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:43:38+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:43:38+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/scratch_rdn.lean`\nTotal Lines: 68\nTotal Bytes: 2360\nShowing lines 1 to 68\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: import Mathlib\n2: import LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\n3: \n4: open SimpleGraph\n5: open GraphCalc\n6: \n7: lemma two_le_romanWeight {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n8:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n9:     (hnt : GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass G) (f : V → Fin 3)\n10:     (hf : GraphCalc.IsRomanDominatingFunction G f) :\n11:     2 ≤ GraphCalc.romanWeight f := by\n12:   unfold GraphCalc.romanWeight\n13:   unfold GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass at hnt\n14:   unfold GraphCalc.order at hnt\n15:   by_contra hc\n16:   have h_le1 : ∑ v : V, (f v : ℕ) ≤ 1 := by omega\n17:   have h_no2 : ∀ v : V, (f v : ℕ) ≠ 2 := by\n18:     intro v hv\n19:     have h_mem := Finset.single_le_sum (fun u _ => Nat.zero_le (f u : ℕ)) (Finset.mem_univ v)\n20:     rw [hv] at h_mem\n21:     omega\n22:   have h_no0 : ∀ v : V, (f v : ℕ) ≠ 0 := by\n23:     intro v hv\n24:     have h_f0 : f v = 0 := by\n25:       ext\n26:       exact hv\n27:     obtain ⟨u, _, hu2⟩ := hf v h_f0\n28:     have hu2_nat : (f u : ℕ) = 2 := by\n29:       rw [hu2]\n30:       rfl\n31:     exact h_no2 u hu2_nat\n32:   have h_ge1 : ∀ v : V, 1 ≤ (f v : ℕ) := by\n33:     intro v\n34:     have h0 := h_no0 v\n35:     omega\n36:   have h_sum_ge : ∑ v : V, 1 ≤ ∑ v : V, (f v : ℕ) :=\n37:     Finset.sum_le_sum (fun v _ => h_ge1 v)\n38:   rw [Finset.sum_const, nsmul_eq_mul, mul_one] at h_sum_ge\n39:   rw [Finset.card_univ] at h_sum_ge\n40:   have h2 : 2 ≤ ∑ v : V, (f v : ℕ) := hnt.trans h_sum_ge\n41:   omega\n42: \n43: lemma two_le_romanDominationNumber {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n44:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n45:     (hnt : GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass G) :\n46:     2 ≤ GraphCalc.romanDominationNumber G := by\n47:   unfold GraphCalc.romanDominationNumber\n48:   let S := (Finset.univ.filter (GraphCalc.IsRomanDominatingFunction G)).image GraphCalc.romanWeight\n49:   have hconst : (fun _ : V => (2 : Fin 3)) ∈ Finset.univ.filter (GraphCalc.IsRomanDominatingFunction G) := by\n50:     rw [Finset.mem_filter]\n51:     refine ⟨Finset.mem_univ _, ?_⟩\n52:     intro v hv\n53:     have h20 : (2 : Fin 3) ≠ 0 := by decide\n54:     exact False.elim (h20 hv)\n55:   have hSne : S.Nonempty := by\n56:     use GraphCalc.romanWeight (fun _ : V => (2 : Fin 3))\n57:     apply Finset.mem_image_of_mem\n58:     exact hconst\n59:   obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := Finset.min_of_nonempty hSne\n60:   rw [hm]\n61:   dsimp\n62:   have hmem : m ∈ S := Finset.mem_of_min hm\n63:   rw [Finset.mem_image] at hmem\n64:   obtain ⟨f, hf, rfl⟩ := hmem\n65:   rw [Finset.mem_filter] at hf\n66:   exact two_le_romanWeight G hnt f hf.2\n67: \n68: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
